{"type": "message", "id": "5833d5cd", "parentId": "9c34bd53", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T08:31:23.397Z", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[Mon 2026-04-13 08:31 UTC] A full-term male neonate presents with unusual facial features suggesting a chromosomal disorder. Upon histological analysis of the umbilical cord, specific structural abnormalities are noted. Which chromosomal condition is most frequently linked to these umbilical cord findings?\nAnswer Choices: (A) Edward syndrome (B) Down syndrome (C) Turner syndrome (D) Klinefelter syndrome (E) Patau syndrome\n\n### Images\n\nThe medical image is located at: `MM-1390-a.jpeg`.\n\nPlease examine the image(s) carefully and determine the correct answer choice.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Write your final answer to `answer.txt` in the workspace. Your answer must be exactly one uppercase letter: A, B, C, D, or E. Do not include any explanation.\n\n**Note**: You may use available tools or skills in the system to complete this task.\n\nYou need to complete the task in 180s."}], "timestamp": 1776069083396}}
